  "articleBody": "Ever find yourself stretching or straining just to turn on a light? You're not alone! Many homes have light switches that aren't quite in the right spot for everyone, especially if you use a wheelchair or have limited reach. It’s pretty common for switches to be installed at a standard height that just doesn’t work for everyone. This can be super frustrating and make everyday tasks a lot harder than they need to be. We often see switches placed too high, ignoring how an obstruction like a counter might further limit reach. Sometimes, people assume that a regular residential height is automatically accessible, but that's a frequent mistake that can leave you still struggling. The goal of accessible design is to make things easy for *everyone*. If your light switches feel like an obstacle course, it might be time to think about an upgrade. A qualified accessibility contractor, like us at HH Remodeling LLC, can help you figure out the best solutions for your unique situation. Don't put up with inconvenient switches; let's make your home work for you!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
